#version 450

// One level of the march carve volume's mip chain (docs/slop/atmosphere_system.md §11, CV3).
//
// **Why the chain exists.** The view march carves cloud shape per sample out of this volume,
// at a world scale that is fixed in metres — so a sample a hundred kilometres away, whose own
// integration step spans a kilometre, was reading a texel eighteen metres across. That is not
// filtering, it is a point sample of a field varying sixty times faster than the sampler, and
// it is what made distant cloud read as white: whichever peaks the lattice happened to land on
// survived the threshold at full strength. The chain gives `cloud.frag` a real band limit to
// select with `textureLod`, which is what a LOD is supposed to be — the previous "LOD" inflated
// the *feature scale* instead, turning distant cumuli into three-to-five kilometre blobs.
//
// **Why a compute pass rather than vkCmdBlitImage.** Two reasons, both about exactness.
// The volume tiles: it is sampled with REPEAT addressing, so its filter must wrap. A blit's
// linear filter clamps at the border instead, which at the coarse levels — where every texel
// *is* a border texel — would leave the tile seam baked into the chain. And a blit's filter is
// a hardware detail; this one is stated. Because every extent here is a power of two, the
// source of a destination texel is exactly the eight texels `2*x + (0,1)^3`, all in range, so
// the wrap the argument above demands costs nothing to honour: there is no edge case to write.
//
// The box average is also what makes the chain *statistically* usable. A level is then the
// conditional expectation of the field over its block, which is an orthogonal projection, so
// the variance the filter removed is exactly `Var(level 0) - Var(level l)` — the quantity
// CloudNoise measures on the host and the carve restates its coverage threshold against.

layout(local_size_x = 4, local_size_y = 4, local_size_z = 4) in;

layout(set = 0, binding = 0, rgba8) uniform readonly image3D source;
layout(set = 0, binding = 1, rgba8) uniform writeonly image3D destination;

layout(push_constant) uniform Params
{
    uint resolution; /**< Destination extent along each axis; the source is twice this. */
} params;

void main()
{
    uvec3 texel = gl_GlobalInvocationID;
    if (any(greaterThanEqual(texel, uvec3(params.resolution))))
        return;

    ivec3 base = ivec3(texel) * 2;
    vec4 sum = vec4(0.0);
    for (int z = 0; z < 2; ++z)
        for (int y = 0; y < 2; ++y)
            for (int x = 0; x < 2; ++x)
                sum += imageLoad(source, base + ivec3(x, y, z));

    imageStore(destination, ivec3(texel), sum * 0.125);
}
